+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `payhook/config.py`: `.env` loader now strips a leading `export `, splits on the first `=` only, removes matching single/double quotes, ignores lines without `=`, and drops ` #` inline comments on unquoted values.
+- `payhook/__main__.py`: new `python -m payhook doctor` prints `KEY = value  [env|.env|default]` for every setting. Unset values show `(not set)`. Secret settings (names containing TOKEN, SECRET, KEY, PASSWORD) are **redacted** (only the length is shown), so output is safe to paste into tickets.
+- `README.md`: documented `doctor`.
+- `tests/test_dotenv_extra.py`: new tests (loader edge cases, doctor redaction/sources). No existing tests touched.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` -> 6 tests, OK (including the 4 pre-existing ones, which now pass).
+- `python -m payhook doctor` in the repo against the real `.env`: quoted/`export` values loaded, sources shown as `.env`, region as `default`.
+- `git status --short`: only README.md, payhook/*, and the new test file show as changed; `.env` is untouched and does not appear as modified/untracked.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not run `git check-ignore .env` (command was not approved); `.env` not showing in `git status` suggests it is ignored, but I did not confirm.
+- Redaction is a deliberate choice: `docs/SUPPORT.md` (step 3) tells support to get the *full API key* in pasted config. That conflicts with `doctor` being safe to paste. `docs/` is outside the files I may change; someone should update that runbook (customers should not paste keys; use the dashboard/account ID instead). If you really want unredacted output, say so.
+- `.env` parsing does not handle escape sequences, multi-line values, or `${VAR}` expansion.
